{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And he said to him, etc. — surely you are my bone, etc.</b> Meaning: he is his bone and he is not his bone, for he perceived that he was not of his dimension — do not imagine in this regard that Lavan is darkness and not light, and therefore he was precise in saying <b>surely my bone</b> in a restrictive sense. Or perhaps he was precise regarding those aspects in which he would resemble him — that they are bone and flesh, not the soul." "<b>Further</b>, he intends to respond to what was intended to inform him that he is a wise man, and he said to him <b>surely my bone</b> — meaning, a diminishment from what he is, on the principle that the Sages of blessed memory stated (Bava Batra 110a) that most sons resemble [their father's family], and one who resembles does not equal the one he resembles in all his parts without one part remaining over. And according to what I explained on the verse (Genesis 27:43) ״בְּרַח לְךָ אֶל לָבָן״ etc. — that he would stand to save him from the hand of Esav — and from the fact that Jacob recounted these matters to Lavan in private, therefore he responded that he would indeed act, for he is his bone and his flesh, and likewise (Job 14:22) — that only his flesh aches upon him, so too upon Jacob: if Esav comes and strikes him, his soul would mourn. And he said <b>surely</b> to qualify — lest he endanger himself for him." "<b>And he stayed with him a month, etc.</b> He prolonged the time for him — perhaps over the course of time his possessions would be revealed, and when he saw that there was no hope of money, he clarified his conduct with him. Further, because he set his eyes upon him to enslave him, he turned a blind eye from him for thirty days and enslaved him for nothing, and only afterward stipulated with him, for the reason that I will explain in his words. Further, he intended to test him whether he would succeed in his way, and you will find that from the day he entered his household he put him to work, and so he himself says ״וַעֲבַדְתַּנִי חִנָּם״ — from this you learn that he had already enslaved him and seen that he was a man who prospers."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:44:40.363500535Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}